### Zuerst GetToken.http ausführen.
GET http://localhost:8080/welcome

###
GET http://localhost:8080/hello
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/hello
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"message":"Hallo LF8"}

###
GET http://localhost:8080/hello?message=Hallo%20LF8
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ID aus der POST-Antwort einsetzen.
GET http://localhost:8080/hello/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ID aus der POST-Antwort einsetzen.
DELETE http://localhost:8080/hello/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET http://localhost:8080/hello/greeting/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET http://localhost:8080/hello/greeting/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET http://localhost:8089/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET http://localhost:8089/qualifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### T007 - Update an existing project (authenticated)

# Replace 1 with the ID of an existing project. All ProjectCreateDto required fields are included.
# Expected: 200 OK with the updated project. The project ID and actualEndDate remain unchanged.
PUT http://localhost:8080/projects/1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "designation": "Rollout Nordlicht aktualisiert",
  "responsibleEmployeeId": 2,
  "customerId": 42,
  "customerContactName": "Mara Beispiel",
  "goalComment": "Geänderter Projektumfang",
  "startDate": "2026-11-05",
  "plannedEndDate": "2027-01-15",
  "requiredQualificationIds": [1, 2]
}

### T006 - Get the employees of a project (authenticated)

# Retrieves the employees assigned to a project with their role.
# Uses the token stored by GetToken.http. Replace 1 with the ID of an existing project.
# Expected: 200 OK with projectId, designation and employees, or an empty list if none are assigned.
GET http://localhost:8080/projects/1/employees
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
